## Two things in this repo that will mislead you

**`tsc --noEmit` is broken by design — do not gate on it.** TypeScript 3.9.10 is declared against
a tsconfig needing 4.1+, so it emits ~2178 errors that are pure noise. The real gate is:

    ./node_modules/.bin/react-scripts build

**CLAUDE.md carries `skip-worktree` in some worktrees, so edits to it silently never commit.**
Measured 2026-11-04: `git ls-files -v CLAUDE.md` returns `H` in `/data/nmechtel/bioimage.io` but
`S` in `.dev/worktree/quick-river`, whose local copy is 207 lines against the committed 106.
Under `S`, git reports the file clean no matter what you write. Check the flag before editing
this file, and edit the copy that reports `H`. Note `.github/copilot-instructions.md` is a
symlink to it, so a committed change here also reaches GitHub Copilot.

